From: ashfordeOU <236818772+ashfordeOU@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:02:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] B5 v2 engine: the v2 area rule behind an explicit selector
 (readings W1 to W3, W10)

src/area_trust.rs: AreaRule (V1 default, V2), raw_state_with, timeline_with and AreaLive::with_rule.
Version 2 makes the area DEGRADED on n_D >= k or n_U >= m, m = 2 for 6 or fewer stations and 1
above (W1). A kshana.area-stations/1 document selects it with "area_rule": "v2" (W3); without
the field the rule is v1 and the bytes are unchanged, on the command line, in Python and in
WebAssembly alike. raw_state, timeline and AreaLive::new keep version 1; v1's tests pass
unchanged. Unit tests: one Untrusted station alone moves an area of 6 or fewer no more, two do (to
UNTRUSTED), above 6 stations v2 is v1, the document field and an unknown rule, and the live path.

tests/area_trust_igs.rs: the T3 run takes KSHANA_B5_AREA_RULE=v2 (W10) and then writes
t3v2_run_<run>.json; without it, v1's run and output are unchanged. No v2 data has been selected,
fetched or scored.
